      "writtenOn": "2025-05-23T19:51:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This all seems like a lot of possible ODR issues for what looks like \"pass a function pointer\". I mean, in G3 an application would need to be super careful that all transitive dependencies (including itself) are using the same one of these. That being said, I understand there are a lot of places a function pointer would need to be passed. On the other hand, said functions pointer / list of codecs could be used by the DirectWrite (currently uses `SkImages::DeferredFromEncodedData`) as well. (FreeType always decodes things itself and has its own special png decoder, and CoreText doesn\u0027t expose anything.)\n\nIs there any reason the DirectWrite approach cannot be used here, and the user can compile in or register whichever PNG decoders they want to use?",
      "revId": "1dd5650ae1a22eb273c93086afc522145850e26e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
